# Jennifer is not a GitHub Linguist language yet. An override naming a language
# Linguist does not know is not a label but an exclusion: the .j files drop out
# of the statistics, and the language bar shows the rest of the repository (Go,
# here). Without the override they are guessed as JASS / Objective-J instead.
#
# Unlike a repository that is almost all Jennifer, this one keeps the other
# languages detectable, so the bar shows the Go interpreter in the meantime. The
# Jennifer line is already right for the day Linguist learns Jennifer. A launcher
# with a jennifer shebang and no extension would need a line of its own; there
# is none here.
*.j linguist-language=Jennifer linguist-detectable=true
